{
	title: 'Opt-in web composer debug log',
	spec: 'config.ason composerDebug (boolean, default false, listed by /config, sent to the page) turns on a web message box probe (src/web/composer-debug.ts). While on, the page records every message box event (beforeinput, input, composition, keys, focus, selection, paste), throttled example changes, size and visual viewport changes, with a snapshot: app.state.text, the box value and selection, the example (classes, cut, text, geometry, font, column width), box/field/attach/action button geometry, viewport and device pixel ratio. Anomalies (logged, not shown): box value differs from app.state.text; the example drawn under typed text; example and box fonts or column widths differ. A 1 s poll records persisting anomalies. Batches of at most 100 rows POST to /composer-debug (a failed upload shows its error in a small fixed badge until one succeeds; logged-in, same-origin, only while the setting is on, under 4 MB); the host appends one JSON line per row to state/composer-debug.log, rotating to .1 past 16 MB. It records draft text, so it stays off unless the user opts in. Diagnoses the invariant that the example never draws under typed text and the box shows app.state.text. The probe caches column measurements per element and font/letter-spacing, invalidating on font load. It samples hint mutations at most once per 250 ms without snapshotting ignored mutations, and its discovery observer ignores its own measurement nodes and unrelated transcript DOM changes. Every user event remains logged.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Bug fix (iOS dictation): dictated text reaches the textarea without input events, so app.state.text lagged the box: the example drew under dictated text, Send/Steer stayed disabled (taps did nothing) or sent stale text. Invariant: before drawing the example or sending, app.state.text equals the box value. Composer syncs on native input, compositionend, keyup, blur, selectionchange while focused, and document-capture pointerdown/touchstart (a disabled button swallows its own pointer events) and before send. The probe also logs every touch/pointer/click/focus event with its target and errors with stacks.',
		'Bug fix (iOS Send taps lost): the probe showed 12 s of Send taps producing no touch, pointer or click event at all while the 44px Send sat on the visual viewport bottom edge, just above the iOS keyboard form bar (iOS 26 Safari, keyboard up). Every tap that reached Send landed 34px or more above that edge. Invariant: on touch screens the composer buttons keep 28px clear of the visual viewport bottom (Composer padding-bottom min 28px). Unconfirmed on device; the probe still logs every touch.',
